ompact" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-twelveMonTrlYld-asOf" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-twelveMonTrlYld-asOf" aria-hidden="true">as of Oct 30, 2026</div></div></div></div><div class="_ws-_spaceXs_1v8bz_37 _ws-_container_1v8bz_25"><div role="list" class="_ws-_dataList_1pwdg_25" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-table-left-column"><div role="listitem" class="_ws-_item_1pwdg_33" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-row-standardDeviation3Yr"><div class="_ws-_d1_1pwdg_43 _ws-"><span class="_ws-oneds-body-s-compact" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-standardDeviation3Yr-label"><span>Standard Deviation<!-- --> </span><span class="_ws-lastword-and-tip"><span>(3y)</span><span class="_ws-tip-inline"><span class="_ws-info-bubble-container _ws-v3design"><button id="infoBubble-f40b6de3-b4e1-40f4-8d23-0b8b970a0694" class="_ws-product-info-bubble _ws-v3design" aria-haspopup="true" aria-label="Standard Deviation (3y) More Info" aria-expanded="false" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-standardDeviation3Yr-infoBubble" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-standardDeviation3Yr-infoBubble" title="Standard deviation measures how dispersed returns are around the average. A higher standard deviation indicates that returns are spread out over a larger range of values and thus, more volatile."><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 18 16" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><g id="Circle-info"><path id="Vector" d="M8 16C10.1217 16 12.1566 15.1571 13.6569 13.6569C15.1571 12.1566 16 10.1217 16 8C16 5.87827 15.1571 3.84344 13.6569 2.34315C12.1566 0.842855 10.1217 0 8 0C5.87827 0 3.84344 0.842855 2.34314 2.34315C0.842853 3.84344 0 5.87827 0 8C0 10.1217 0.842853 12.1566 2.34314 13.6569C3.84344 15.1571 5.87827 16 8 16ZM6.75 10.5H7.5V8.5H6.75H6V7H6.75H8.25H9V7.75V10.5H9.25H10V12H9.25H6.75H6V10.5H6.75ZM9 6H7V4H9V6Z" fill="black"></path></g></svg></button></span></span></span></span></div><div class="_ws-_d2_1pwdg_51"><span class="_ws-oneds-body-m-compact-bold" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-standardDeviation3Yr-data" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-standardDeviation3Yr">13.35%</span></div><div class="_ws-oneds-body-xs-compact _ws-_d3_1pwdg_60" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-standardDeviation3Yr-asOf" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-standardDeviation3Yr-asOf">as of<!-- --> <!-- -->Sep 30, 2026</div></div><div role="listitem" class="_ws-_item_1pwdg_33" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-row-weightedAvgCouponFi"><div class="_ws-_d1_1pwdg_43 _ws-"><span class="_ws-oneds-body-s-compact" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-weightedAvgCouponFi-label"><span>Weighted Avg<!-- --> </span><span class="_ws-lastword-and-tip"><span>Coupon</span><span class="_ws-tip-inline"><span class="_ws-info-bubble-container _ws-v3design"><button id="infoBubble-efa45b15-898b-440c-89a6-9dbc9e7c595e" class="_ws-product-info-bubble _ws-v3design" aria-haspopup="true" aria-label="Weighted Avg Coupon More Info" aria-expanded="false" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-weightedAvgCouponFi-infoBubble" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-weightedAvgCouponFi-infoBubble" title="The average coupon rate of the underlying bonds in the fund, weighted by each bond&#x27;s face value."><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 18 16" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><g id="Circle-info"><path id="Vector" d="M8 16C10.1217 16 12.1566 15.1571 13.6569 13.6569C15.1571 12.1566 16 10.1217 16 8C16 5.87827 15.1571 3.84344 13.6569 2.34315C12.1566 0.842855 10.1217 0 8 0C5.87827 0 3.84344 0.842855 2.34314 2.34315C0.842853 3.84344 0 5.87827 0 8C0 10.1217 0.842853 12.1566 2.34314 13.6569C3.84344 15.1571 5.87827 16 8 16ZM6.75 10.5H7.5V8.5H6.75H6V7H6.75H8.25H9V7.75V10.5H9.25H10V12H9.25H6.75H6V10.5H6.75ZM9 6H7V4H9V6Z" fill="black"></path></g></svg></button></span></span></span></span></div><div class="_ws-_d2_1pwdg_51"><span class="_ws-oneds-body-m-compact-bold" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-weightedAvgCouponFi-data" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-weightedAvgCouponFi">3.38</span></div><div class="_ws-oneds-body-xs-compact _ws-_d3_1pwdg_60" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-weightedAvgCouponFi-asOf" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-weightedAvgCouponFi-asOf">as of<!-- --> <!-- -->Oct 30, 2026</div></div><div role="listitem" class="_ws-_item_1pwdg_33" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-row-modelOad"><div class="_ws-_d1_1pwdg_43 _ws-"><span class="_ws-oneds-body-s-compact" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-modelOad-label"><span>Effective<!-- --> </span><span class="_ws-lastword-and-tip"><span>Duration</span><span class="_ws-tip-inline"><span class="_ws-info-bubble-container _ws-v3design"><button id="infoBubble-9f4bee03-ed0c-477a-8b36-41469258fa21" class="_ws-product-info-bubble _ws-v3design" aria-haspopup="true" aria-label="Effective Duration More Info" aria-expanded="false" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-modelOad-infoBubble" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-modelOad-infoBubble" title="Effective Duration measures the sensitivity of the price of a bond with or without embedded options to changes in interest rates, taking into account the likelihood of the bond being called, put and/or sunk prior to its final maturity date while incorporating after-tax impacts on the bond. The options-based duration model used by BlackRock employs certain assumptions and may differ from other fund complexes. Effective Duration is measured at the individual bond level, aggregated to the portfolio level, and adjusted for leverage, hedging transactions and non-bond holdings, including derivatives."><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 18 16" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><g id="Circle-info"><path id="Vector" d="M8 16C10.1217 16 12.1566 15.1571 13.6569 13.6569C15.1571 12.1566 16 10.1217 16 8C16 5.87827 15.1571 3.84344 13.6569 2.34315C12.1566 0.842855 10.1217 0 8 0C5.87827 0 3.84344 0.842855 2.34314 2.34315C0.842853 3.84344 0 5.87827 0 8C0 10.1217 0.842853 12.1566 2.34314 13.6569C3.84344 15.1571 5.87827 16 8 16ZM6.75 10.5H7.5V8.5H6.75H6V7H6.75H8.25H9V7.75V10.5H9.25H10V12H9.25H6.75H6V10.5H6.75ZM9 6H7V4H9V6Z" fill="black"></path></g></svg></button></span></span></span></span></div><div class="_ws-_d2_1pwdg_51"><span class="_ws-oneds-body-m-compact-bold" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-modelOad-data" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-modelOad">14.83 yrs</span></div><div class="_ws-oneds-body-xs-compact _ws-_d3_1pwdg_60" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-modelOad-asOf" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-modelOad-asOf">as of<!-- --> <!-- -->Oct 30, 2026</div></div><div role="listitem" class="_ws-_item_1pwdg_33" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-row-optionAdjustedSpread"><div class="_ws-_d1_1pwdg_43 _ws-"><span class="_ws-oneds-body-s-compact" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-optionAdjustedSpread-label"><span>Option Adjusted<!-- --> </span><span class="_ws-lastword-and-tip"><span>Spread</span><span class="_ws-tip-inline"><span class="_ws-info-bubble-container _ws-v3design"><button id="infoBubble-bb148fbe-5e45-4d3d-b894-8f940f7fa5a8" class="_ws-product-info-bubble _ws-v3design" aria-haspopup="true" aria-label="Option Adjusted Spread More Info" aria-expanded="false" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-optionAdjustedSpread-infoBubble" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-optionAdjustedSpread-infoBubble" title="The weighted average incremental yield earned over similar duration matched US Treasuries for taxable fixed income or the AAA-rated Municipal Yield Curve for tax-exempt municipals, measured in basis points (one basis point is equivalent to 0.01% or 0.0001). This metric considers the likelihood that bonds will be called or prepaid before the scheduled maturity date."><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 18 16" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><g id="Circle-info"><path id="Vector" d="M8 16C10.1217 16 12.1566 15.1571 13.6569 13.6569C15.1571 12.1566 16 10.1217 16 8C16 5.87827 15.1571 3.84344 13.6569 2.34315C12.1566 0.842855 10.1217 0 8 0C5.87827 0 3.84344 0.842855 2.34314 2.34315C0.842853 3.84344 0 5.87827 0 8C0 10.1217 0.842853 12.1566 2.34314 13.6569C3.84344 15.1571 5.87827 16 8 16ZM6.75 10.5H7.5V8.5H6.75H6V7H6.75H8.25H9V7.75V10.5H9.25H10V12H9.25H6.75H6V10.5H6.75ZM9 6H7V4H9V6Z" fill="black"></path></g></svg></button></span></span></span></span></div><div class="_ws-_d2_1pwdg_51"><span class="_ws-oneds-body-m-compact-bold" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-optionAdjustedSpread-data" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-optionAdjustedSpread">-0.13 bps</span></div><div class="_ws-oneds-body-xs-compact _ws-_d3_1pwdg_60" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-optionAdjustedSpread-asOf" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-optionAdjustedSpread-asOf">as of<!-- --> <!-- -->Oct 30, 2026</div></div></div><div role="list" class="_ws-_dataList_1pwdg_25 _ws-_reverseStripe_1pwdg_78 _ws-_firstDataListEven_1pwdg_85" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-table-right-column"><div role="listitem" class="_ws-_item_1pwdg_33" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-row-beta3Yr"><div class="_ws-_d1_1pwdg_43 _ws-"><span class="_ws-oneds-body-s-compact" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-beta3Yr-label"><span>Equity Beta<!-- --> </span><span class="_ws-lastword-and-tip"><span>(3y)</span><span class="_ws-tip-inline"><span class="_ws-info-bubble-container _ws-v3design"><button id="infoBubble-d22b00a5-a157-4013-ba12-74b0b95ae298" class="_ws-product-info-bubble _ws-v3design" aria-haspopup="true" aria-label="Equity Beta (3y) More Info" aria-expanded="false" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-beta3Yr-infoBubble" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-beta3Yr-infoBubble" title="Beta is a measure of the tendency of securities to move with the market as a whole. A beta of 1 indicates that the security&#x27;s price will move with the market. A beta less than 1 indicates the security tends to be less volatile than the market, while a beta greater than 1 indicates the security is more volatile than the market.Calculated vs. S&amp;P 500"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 18 16" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><g id="Circle-info"><path id="Vector" d="M8 16C10.1217 16 12.1566 15.1571 13.6569 13.6569C15.1571 12.1566 16 10.1217 16 8C16 5.87827 15.1571 3.84344 13.6569 2.34315C12.1566 0.842855 10.1217 0 8 0C5.87827 0 3.84344 0.842855 2.34314 2.34315C0.842853 3.84344 0 5.87827 0 8C0 10.1217 0.842853 12.1566 2.34314 13.6569C3.84344 15.1571 5.87827 16 8 16ZM6.75 10.5H7.5V8.5H6.75H6V7H6.75H8.25H9V7.75V10.5H9.25H10V12H9.25H6.75H6V10.5H6.75ZM9 6H7V4H9V6Z" fill="black"></path></g></svg></button></span></span></span></span></div><div class="_ws-_d2_1pwdg_51"><span class="_ws-oneds-body-m-compact-bold" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-beta3Yr-data" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-beta3Yr">0.54</span></div><div class="_ws-oneds-body-xs-compact _ws-_d3_1pwdg_60" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-beta3Yr-asOf" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-beta3Yr-asOf">as of<!-- --> <!-- -->Sep 30, 2026</div></div><div role="listitem" class="_ws-_item_1pwdg_33" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-row-fxHedgedYield"><div class="_ws-_d1_1pwdg_43 _ws-"><span class="_ws-oneds-body-s-compact" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-fxHedgedYield-label"><span>Average Yield to<!-- --> </span><span class="_ws-lastword-and-tip"><span>Maturity</span><span class="_ws-tip-inline"><span class="_ws-info-bubble-container _ws-v3design"><button id="infoBubble-eb1c8c49-4c70-4094-b64f-a74b23355a67" class="_ws-product-info-bubble _ws-v3design" aria-haspopup="true" aria-label="Average Yield to Maturity More Info" aria-expanded="false" data-id="fundamentalsAndRisk-fxHedgedYield-infoBubble" webqc-datapoint="fundamentalsAndRisk-fxHedgedYield-infoBubble" title="Yield to Maturity is the discount rate that equates the present value of a bond&#x27;s cash flows with its market price (including accrued interest). For callable bonds, this yield is the yield to worst. For TIPS, this yield includes the market&#x27;s estimates for inflation over the life of the bond. For FX positions, this yield includes the carry yield from currency positions, calculated based on an estimated annualized 1m forward contract. The measure does not incl